extend type Mutation {
  """Appends technology to the named force's research queue (force defaults to player, and both force and technology must be non-empty and exist). The technology must be enabled, not already researched, and not rejected by the engine; a missing prerequisite, an unknown force or an already researched or disabled technology is a GraphQL error before the queue changes, and an unmet prerequisite error names every prerequisite that is not researched yet, so a successful call always reports started=true. The returned state holds tick, the technology name, the force's currentResearch (the running technology, or null), and researchQueue in engine order after the append; in Factorio 2.0 the first researchQueue entry is the technology currently being researched, so it repeats currentResearch. Emits one in-game notification unless message overrides it."""
  queueResearch(input: QueueResearchInput!): ResearchState!
  """Empties the force research queue while leaving the technology that is currently being researched running, reporting tick and the state read after the write. In Factorio 2.0 an empty research_queue cancels the running research, so the engine write keeps exactly that technology as the sole queue entry instead of writing an empty list; currentResearch, technology and started therefore describe the research that is still running after the call. When the force has no running research nothing is queued. force defaults to player and must exist. The returned researchQueue is empty only when no research is running; otherwise it holds the kept technology, because the first queue entry is the current research. Emits one in-game notification unless message overrides it."""
  clearResearchQueue(input: ResearchQueueInput!): ResearchState!
  """Sandbox shortcut that unlocks every technology on the named force at once: RESEARCH calls the engine's research_all_technologies to apply full research effects, ENABLE only enables the prototypes without those effects. force must exist and mode must be RESEARCH or ENABLE; engine failure is a GraphQL error. Returns the tick, force, mode, and the count of technologies whose researched (RESEARCH) or enabled (ENABLE) flag is true after the call, so the number reflects the whole force rather than this call's delta. Emits one in-game notification unless message overrides it."""
  unlockAllTechnologies(input: UnlockTechnologiesInput!): ResearchUnlockResult!
  """:writes one recipe's unlocked flag on a force without researching anything else, which is the narrow sandbox alternative to unlockAllTechnologies when a single recipe is blocked by an engine trigger that scripting cannot satisfy (for example the build-entity trigger of space-science-pack, whose asteroid-collector cannot be built from script on a space platform). force and recipe must exist, enabled is written straight to LuaRecipe.enabled, and the returned snapshot reads the flag back in the same tick. This is a sandbox shortcut: it neither applies research effects nor marks any technology researched, so a recipe can become craftable while its technology stays unresearched."""
  setRecipeEnabled(input: RecipeEnabledInput!): RecipeEnabledResult!
}

"""Set one recipe's unlocked flag on a force without researching its technology."""
input RecipeEnabledInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  recipe: String!
  enabled: Boolean!
  """Print this text in-game to all connected players instead of the generated notification."""
  message: String
}

"""Post-write recipe unlock state."""
type RecipeEnabledResult {
  tick: Float!
  force: String!
  recipe: String!
  enabled: Boolean!
}

"""technology must be a non-empty name of an existing technology on the force."""
input QueueResearchInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  technology: String!
  """Print this text in-game to all connected players instead of the generated notification."""
  message: String
}

input ResearchQueueInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  """Print this text in-game to all connected players instead of the generated notification."""
  message: String
}

input UnlockTechnologiesInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  mode: TechnologyUnlockMode! = RESEARCH
  """Print this text in-game to all connected players instead of the generated notification."""
  message: String
}

enum TechnologyUnlockMode {
  """Apply full research effects as if every technology were researched."""
  RESEARCH
  """Enable the technology prototypes without applying research effects."""
  ENABLE
}

type ResearchUnlockResult {
  tick: Float!
  force: String!
  mode: TechnologyUnlockMode!
  technologies: Int!
}
